      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "description": "agent_psi_tool_full: the fraction of the trailing 60s in which EVERY ACTIVE agent in the scope was inside a tool call. This is PSI `full` — a unanimity signal, normalized over the active agents only — so with a single active worker it saturates at 100% by construction, and it collapses toward 0 when several workers are in different states. It answers 'is tool time blocking the whole scope at once', NOT 'how busy is the fleet'. For occupancy read the mean-concurrent-agents panels below."
    },
