      },
      "description": "THE headline view: what the sub-agent fleet's time is actually going to, as a stack of MEAN CONCURRENT AGENTS per state over a 60s window. The stack HEIGHT is the mean number of agents present (busy + idle), so the y-axis is agents, not a percentage: one busy worker reads 1.0, four read 4.0. That is the whole point of the unit. This panel used to stack agent_psi_*_full, which CANNOT express fleet composition: `full` is a PSI unanimity signal normalized over the ACTIVE agents, so a single tool-bound worker rendered as a 100%-tool fleet, and — the converse, measured on this fleet — four workers in four different states collapsed every band toward zero at peak concurrency. Bands: INFERENCE (green) productive generation. STALLED (red) blocked but generating nothing — 529 / 429 back-off, network, TTFT, queueing; pair it with the per-model API-error panel below to see WHICH model and WHY. TOOL (blue) inside a tool call. OVERHEAD (yellow) between-turn bookkeeping. UNOBSERVABLE (magenta) no transcript write for AGENT_PSI_STALE_AFTER_SECONDS while last seen working: a suspended host and a runaway blocking command are indistinguishable from a transcript, and this band is that admission, not a claim the agent is gone. IDLE (grey) parked between turns; WAITING (cyan) blocked on a human. Main loop excluded — it has its own panel."
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Main vs fleet — busy / idle / unobservable agents (60s)",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum without (state) (agent_psi_mean_agents{scope=\"fleet\",window=\"60\",model=\"all\",state=~\"inference|inference_stalled|tool|overhead\"})",
