          },
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "calcs": [
            "max",
            "sum"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "description": "Observed API-error entries per MODEL and CAUSE over a trailing 5m window — the per-model upstream-impact signal, and the input to model-routing policy. Model families are provisioned and rate-limited independently, so the actionable statement is 'opus took N capacity errors in this window while fable took none', which a model=all aggregate cannot make. CAUSES are separated because they are different knobs: capacity (529 / 5xx / overloaded — the provider is out of headroom; knob = which model, when, retry budget), rate_limit (429 / quota — knob = our concurrency and fleet size), network (transport failed before a verdict — ours to chase), context_overflow (prompt too long — self-inflicted, and the direct outcome of an opus-vs-sonnet routing choice, so it must never read as provider trouble), other (recognised but unmatched — visible on purpose). Refusals and auth failures are filtered out here: neither is a performance signal. These are counts of OBSERVED events only — the task-level cost of a retry (an agent dying and being respawned) needs cross-agent semantics this layer does not have, and is not modelled here. Both fleet and main scopes are summed, so the dispatcher's own errors are included."
    },
